# SPL (1) queues the next cell then the imp; JMP #0 (2); the imp at cell 2 copies itself to 3 (3);
# JMP (4); the imp at 3 copies itself to 4 (5). Both processes live on.
golden: bbctests/examples/spl_two_processes.bbc
# a lone imp (no SPL) would already have copied itself at instruction 2: with SPL it is the JMP's turn
cell 2 3 DAT.F $0, $0
cell 3 3 MOV.I $0, $1
cell 5 4 MOV.I $0, $1
alive 1000
